===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|India|transitive}} To [[act]] as a [[#Noun|shroff]], [[especially]] {{lb|en|historical}} to [[inspect]] [[coin]]s to [[detect]] [[debasement]], [[counterfeit]]s, [[clip]]ping, [[&c.]] for a [[commission]].
#* '''1757''' July 7, {{w|Robert Clive}}, letter, cited in John Malcolm, ''Life of Robert, Lord Clive'', Vol. I, p. 278:
#*: I represented... that the money could not be divided till it was '''shroffed'''.
#* '''1906''' April 14, ''Saturday Review'', p. 451:
#*: The potential revenues of China are immense, but they are ‘'''shroffed'''’... by every hand through which they pass.

